<edge source="global_finance_shift::oil_price_level" target="ai_governance::development_pace" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in global oil prices increases energy, cooling and logistics costs for hyperscalers and cloud providers, prompting reductions or rescheduling of high‑cost compute workloads and thereby slowing model training and feature rollouts.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::oil_price_level" target="middle_east_chokepoints::maritime_attack_freq" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher crude prices raise the value of tanker cargoes and rents from seizing or interdicting shipments, increasing incentives for state proxies, militias and criminal groups to mount attacks on commercial shipping.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::oil_price_level" target="middle_east_chokepoints::infra_outage_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated oil prices increase the payoff from sabotaging pipelines, terminals and export infrastructure, prompting more targeted attacks and rent-seeking disruptions of facilities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_strike_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher crude prices increase the economic value of energy infrastructure and, through higher state and criminal rents, provide both the incentive and financing to mount attacks against production, storage and transport facilities in the theater.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::oil_price_level" target="tech_supply_divide::ai_compute_demand" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained increase in oil (and related energy/transport) prices raises operational costs for power‑intensive AI training and for moving hardware, causing firms to reduce or postpone large training runs and thereby cutting immediate compute demand.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
