<edge source="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_level" target="ai_governance::investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in policy interest rates raises the cost of borrowing and increases discount rates for investors and VC funds, causing immediate pull‑backs or down‑valuations of capital committed to high‑burn, long‑horizon frontier AI projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_level" target="middle_east_chokepoints::market_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter policy rates raise borrowing and hedging costs and reduce market liquidity, causing insurers, traders and investors to demand wider risk premia on oil and shipping exposures.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_price_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in short-term policy rates depresses aggregate demand and freight/industrial activity within months, reducing near‑term energy consumption and easing price and supply pressure on energy markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_level" target="tech_supply_divide::cloud_utilization" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher short‑term policy rates raise corporate borrowing costs and tighten working‑capital budgets, prompting enterprises to defer non‑critical cloud deployments and scale‑ups, which lowers near‑term cloud capacity utilization.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_supply_divide</data>
</edge>
