<edge source="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_expectations" target="ai_governance::development_pace" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger market expectations of higher future policy rates lead firms to reprioritise short‑term profitability over long, compute‑intensive R&amp;D, delaying large training runs and hiring and thus slowing the pace of frontier model development.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_expectations" target="tech_supply_divide::ai_development_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Market expectations of tighter policy lead venture investors and corporate CFOs to reprice risk and conserve cash, directly slowing hiring, project starts and model development budgets in the near term.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_finance_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_supply_divide</data>
</edge>
