<edge source="tech_supply_divide::infra_capital_flow" target="ai_governance::investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Visible, large investments into AI infrastructure lower marginal training costs and signal commercial viability, directly attracting additional finance into frontier model R&amp;D and commercialization by improving expected returns on upstream bets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_supply_divide</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_supply_divide::infra_capital_flow" target="global_finance_shift::long_term_govt_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in capital directed to AI data centers and related fixed assets leads firms and municipalities to issue more long-dated debt and reallocates investor demand away from sovereign bonds, exerting upward pressure on benchmark long-term yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_supply_divide</data>
  <data key="d39">global_finance_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_supply_divide::infra_capital_flow" target="global_finance_shift::policy_rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated investment spending in AI infrastructure boosts near‑term aggregate demand and input-price pressures (construction, electricity, semiconductors), prompting markets to revise up expected central-bank tightening over the policy horizon.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_supply_divide</data>
  <data key="d39">global_finance_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_supply_divide::infra_capital_flow" target="middle_east_chokepoints::naval_presence_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased investment in AI/compute infrastructure funds procurement and deployment of maritime ISR, long‑endurance drones and autonomous surface/underwater craft by states and private security firms, enabling more persistent patrols and higher deployed naval/maritime security presence around chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_supply_divide</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_supply_divide::infra_capital_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_capability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased capital directed to AI infrastructure enables procurement of high‑end accelerators, datacenter capacity and MLOps services used by defense contractors and startups, accelerating development, autonomy and operational deployment of long‑range unmanned strike systems and swarm coordination.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
